  "repo_truth": "The parent submits an immutable 43-path HCM-2.3 implementation subject. The subject reports focused and workspace proof, one explicitly user-authorized CRITICAL source-kind schema-root separation, and bounded registry-brief real-path status. These are claims for independent verification, not a success conclusion.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 43 manifest hashes, ordinal ordering, aggregate fingerprint, active-dispatch exclusion, dispatch schema, selected handoff, and branch/HEAD authority before review.",
    "Review every changed production, test, fixture, control-pack, implementation-dispatch, and proof path in the immutable subject against the complete HCM-2.3 packet and runtime contracts.",
    "Review correctness, readability/simplicity, architecture, security, performance, dependency discipline, source-kind schema containment, safe repository I/O, persistence/recovery, idempotency, and CLI exit/output behavior.",
    "Return evidence-backed findings ordered Critical, Required, Optional, Nit with exact file/line evidence, failure mode, smallest authority-preserving repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, branch changes, preservation/archive access, or user task hops.",
    "No HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, Phase 4 SDK/transport, package-default expansion, resolver redesign, built-in namespace expansion, or HCM-2.2 reinterpretation.",
    "Do not accept passing tests or the proof narrative as a success conclusion; verify implementation and tests independently."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke the required skills, read repository AGENTS.md and the complete dispatch, and return BLOCKED on any manifest, branch, HEAD, handoff, or authority mismatch.",
    "Review tests first and map every mandatory HCM-2.3 and user-authorized schema-root behavior to an effective regression that would fail for the wrong implementation.",
    "Audit the fixed compile-time BuiltIn definitions/schemas domain, allowlist-only bytes, request-root-only Repository domain, containment-before-cache/I/O/error precedence, and unchanged high-level schema resolver.",
    "Audit exact selection closure, generic operation context, canonical YAML, safe canonical reads, pure intake evaluation, immutable lineage, crash recovery, refusal establishment/replay, idempotency retention, zero-write validation, compare-and-write promotion, and process concurrency.",
    "Audit the actual CLI boundary for ten fixed commands, required explicit authority, stable exits, JSON/human rendering, path/stdin handling, no direct writes, no raw-key disclosure, and no per-kind/example dispatch.",
    "Audit the large new modules for unnecessary complexity, duplicated owner algorithms, hidden fallbacks, dead code, unsafe or unbounded filesystem work, lock-order/reentrancy bugs, and structural remedies within the authorized production scope.",
    "Verify control-pack classifications move only the exact registry-brief subsets, broader gates remain open, and no package definition, Cargo/dependency, HCM-2.2, HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, SDK/transport, archive, or preservation path changed.",
    "Return CLEAN only with zero Critical, Required, Optional, and Nit findings; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repairing files."
  ],
